{color:#333333}Please find some comments below from my side. I'm expected to deliver the contract draft as soon as possible, to send it to the legal team at PWC. If needed later, we can schedule a call between both teams.{color} 
* {color:#333333}

PwC shall not sign up for access to the Business Portal, incl shall not enter the B4B Agreement under the T&C. (PWC will sign up to multiple single Business Portal Accounts, this solution will be temporary until we can migrate to a different type of system, centralizing all invoices into one platform with individual cards associated to the global account);{color}
* {color:#333333}

PwC shall:{color}
** {color:#333333}

provide a list of emails of employees who shall sign up for a regular Bolt Passenger account and create themselves a Work profile. What if the Passenger already has a Bolt Passenger account connected to his/her phone No, or s/he wants to have a Passenger account for private purposes? Does this employee need to have more than one phone No? Why don't we agree instead that PwC shall just provide a list of emails which their employees add to their Work profile for sending the invoices to, and we'll use this as basis for any further invoicing, cashbacks etc? (For GDPR reasons, PWC won’t provide a list of emails for us to have track, the way we are going to do this track will be through creating various B4B accounts (example, with the name PWC France), and this way we can track through looker their monthly usage, and by the end of the year, proceed to a Cashback according with this data){color}
** {color:#333333}

pay for the rides done using the email address named above by using the post payment method as described in clause 4.17 etc in the B4B T&C. Or is there a reason why we do not want or need to agree on the exact payment method up front? ( users will associate their personal/business cards to their b4b accounts);{color}
* {color:#333333}

Bolt shall:{color}
** {color:#333333}

provide PwC a summarizing report (incl data on total No of trips and total amount of Fare) for all the Work profile rides done under respective Passenger accounts.{color} 
** {color:#333333}

provide a 3% cashback for a full calendar year of cooperation (i.e no cashback if Agreement has lasted less than one full calendar year in any way? So PwC gets cashback if the agreement is valid from Jan 1st 2021 to Dec 31st 2021, but not if from Jan 2nd 2021 to Dec 30th 2022?) by 31st of January of n+1 (PWC will get a 3% cashback regardless of the starting date , example for this year if they start operating with us in February, the agreement will go from February till December 2021){color}
** {color:#333333}

provide -30% of discount for all PWC employees on their non Work profile rides for the first 5 trips taken (available for the 1st 3 months since respective comms - i.e push notification? I trust we have log to prove the time of such push?). Is it at all doable if the Passengers are required to sign up for a separate Passenger account? (This procedure will be executed through a single Promocode to all PWC employees (6000), Marketing is already involved and everything aligned operationally).{color}


{color:#333333}And as heads up, the above necessarily doesn't cover all the details yet. Legal has not facilitated Work profile in such manner before, but I expect we're able to reuse B4B T&C in many aspects though, foremost clause 4 (Payments), but also for personal liability, term and termination, final provisions, data processing, confidentiality.{color} 

{color:#333333}Yet all in all requires drafting a contract from scratch.{color}

