Hello,

I thought a lot today about this again. I wrote to you on Slack as well.

The agreement is valid until 21.03.22. We have to inform them at least one month before this term in order not to continue it automatically for another year, meaning no later than 21.02.22. COVIDs situation is not getting better. No written plans by the government on that, but I've discussed with the biggest entertainment venue in LT whether they have some inside info on when the restrictions for events could be released so  *optimistic* scenario is:
* January still under restrictions, no events at all
* in February up to 300 people could be allowed (last time we had the same situation, we agreed with Siemens arena (Universali arena) not to pay because it's too small and inadequate audience for that amount of money)
* in March the restrictions could be lifted a bit up to 1000 people meaning we would probably have to pay for the services if there will be some events happening.

So I think now that it is not worth risking with that termination before the actual termination time as we will probably not renew any payments until March.
In January we just could send them the note that after the period is over, we are not willing to continue further. In this way we will keep a better relationship with them, will not get into arguments (because its really hard to predict the reaction). Moreover, the owners of the arena changed during the last few weeks. So all my assumptions from the past behaviour of theirs now can be wrong. Worst case scenario, we would pay 800 eur for one last month of services if the restrictions will be lifted in March. But it is not as risky as trying to terminate it and go into argument with the second biggest venue in LT which is a good channel during good times (not covid).

Still answering your questions if we'd proceed:
- The termination date could be January 1st
- There's no penalty described in the contract. Only, in case of breach of contract:
 {color:#172b4d} _{color}{color:#333333} _In case of a breach, there is 4.4.:_{color}{color:#172b4d}{color} {color:#172b4d}{color}
{color:#172b4d}{color}  _{color:#172b4d} _4.4. If one of the Parties fails to fulfill its obligations under this Agreement or performs them improperly, the other Party shall submit in writing a claim for a breach. If the improperly performing Party does not start to properly perform obligations or does not correct violations within 5 (five) working days from the claim, the other Party shall have the right to terminate this Agreement by giving written notice to the breaching Party before 10 (ten) calendar days. Upon termination of the Agreement on the basis of this clause, the faulting Party, as soon as possible, but in any case no later than within 3 (three) calendar days upon receipt of the notification, shall pay the other Party a fine of EUR 250 (two hundred and fifty euros) and reimburse all other Direct losses incurred by a party, to the extent that they are not covered by the fine paid._{color}


And there's also 4.3.:
 _4.3. The Agreement may be terminated before its expiration by mutual consent of the Parties in a separate act, all claims between the Parties under the Agreement and its annexes shall be resolved and the consequences of this fact shall be specified in that act._



- No payments. We pay invoices according to the schedule plus we've suspended the agreement now for a while.{color:#000000}
