[^Annex 2. Summary.final.docx]

ALGORITHM=INSTANT

Operations only modify metadata in the data dictionary
No exclusive metadata locks are taken on the table during preparation and execution
The table data is unaffected
Introduced in MySQL 8.0.12
If the ALGORITHM clause is omitted, MySQL uses ALGORITHM=INSTANT for storage engines
Prority: INSTANT > INPLACE > COPY

Specifying an ALGORITHM clause means run or fail with an error otherwise
ALGORITHM=DEFAULT is the same as omitting

Supported operations.

# Adding column (Limitation apply)
# Adding or dropping a virtual column
# Adding or dropping a column default value
# Modifying the definition of an ENUM or SET column (Limitation apply)
# Changing the index type
# Renaming a table (Limitation apply)

Limitation
[https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.0/en/innodb-online-ddl-operations.html|https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.0/en/innodb-online-ddl-operations.html]

INFORMATION_SCHEMA.INNODB_TABLES and INFORMATION_SCHEMA.INNODB_COLUMNS provide metadata for instantly added columns.
INFORMATION_SCHEMA.INNODB_TABLES.INSTANT_COLS shows number of columns in the table prior to adding the first instant column.
INFORMATION_SCHEMA.INNODB_COLUMNS.HAS_DEFAULT and DEFAULT_VALUE provide metadata about default values for instantly added columns. 

