So. It came back in an unexpected way. And I haven't managed to follow up on this since Monday,,, 

1. Turns out the agreement text (clause 4.1.) says it is valid for one year and if we do not terminate it, it continues automatically. 
2. Clause 3.1. sets the price "for the whole agreement period" – 9600 Eur (800/months, 12 months).
3. However, the Annex where the advertising services are listed, is said to be agreed for 3 years (2019.03.22 – 2022.03.22) but the final amount for these 3 years is also 9600 Eur. The agreement contains mistakes. Siemens arena said that there was a mistake in that clause 4.1. as that it was actually agreed for 3 years and they did give Bolt a better offer because we agreed for 3 year period. Plus, it is the 2nd year as this agreement is valid, so they've been following the 3-year logic here. 

As the amount everywhere in the agreement is listed for one year (9600) I believe there was a mistake only in the date 2019.03.22 –  *2022.03.22.* 

Siemens arena's position now: surely, they want to live this year with us as well until 2022. Now it is not a big deal as the services are stopped and will not be launched until the restrictions are over (which may happen only in autumn probably...). Therefore we would need a really strong negotiation here, and it is still not unclear how long the agreement was intended to be signed, so many interpretations can be raised.
My position: mixed feelings. We could argue now, as the final price is for one year and every other clause matches the 1 year idea, except the Annex. On the other side, since the services are stopped, we do not have expenses here, we can wait until restrictions were over and be present there for 800/month in autumn (maybe more events will come) or we can ask for a reduction on monthly fee because of less events or limited number of audience (following what happened after the first lockdown wave). This one may cost us a bit for the months left after quarantine but we can also have coverage as well and we do not need to start over with the advertising material and so on... 

Siemens arena is the place we definitely want to be seen when there are enough events and audience as this is the biggest venue in the capital.

