Hello [~accountid:5ae966399abb77267ba68b16],

Indexes in MySQL 5.7 are always ASCending, thus this is redundant:

{code:sql}
UNIQUE KEY `support_case_idx_unique` (`support_case_id`),
INDEX `support_case_idx` (`support_case_id` ASC))
{code}
https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/5.7/en/create-index.html

{noformat}
A key_part specification can end with ASC or DESC. These keywords are permitted for future extensions for specifying ascending or descending index value storage. Currently, they are parsed but ignored; index values are always stored in ascending order.
{noformat}


I propose only creating `support_case_idx_unique` and removing `support_case_idx` from change request. 
Are you okay with that?

