Hope the below brings some clarity on where we are with this. 

First and foremost, we have in place technical controls for customer debt never getting out of hands (see also clause 4.18 etc{color} [{color:#333333}in the T&C{color}|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/terms-for-business/]{color:#333333}). And of course our current agreements with customers (foremost the B4B T&C) provide the legal basis to claim for overdue payment.  

So the question is indeed about the technical side, i.e how do we actually collect the debt, and the respective procedures.  

Now, on to your questions. 
{color}
* {color:#333333} *What legal actions or procedures or framework to proceed with the collection/ recovery of the debt (unpaid obligations, negative balance) are in place? What can be added or is planned to be added?* 


B4B team has set up the following thumb rules (see foremost in the very end):{color} [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BFB/pages/2235859265/Credit+Payment+Terms|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BFB/pages/2235859265/Credit+Payment+Terms]{color:#333333} 

So fair to say we have no sophisticated debt management framework as such in place. It was discussed already in the end of 2018 ahead of the first launch, but was deprioritized due to low relevance - indeed, also the info I got from @amy few months ago indicated only ca EUR 150k worth of overdue payments globally. Also, I have no info on any B4B debt collection request ever having been elevated to Legal. 

That said, I’d firstly direct this question to B4B team - if and what’s the priority of setting up (more sophisticated) framework either per market/ regionally/ globally? @amy{color} 

[{color:#333333}Yury Koshelyuk{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5f1a8c60591bbc001bec874d]{color:#333333} unfortunately I don’t have access to the links you shared. 
{color}
* {color:#333333} *What "fear factors" as result of framework do Bolt has and can use in communication (report to credit bureaus, tax office, police, etc)?* 


Can be discussed, but foremost we’d need to set up a proper civil framework if needed, typically this means: internal steps/ debt collection agency/ court proceedings/ bailiff.
 Very high-level, then likely we’d want to outsource this as far as possible as experience shows that such debt management procedures would create considerable overhead which I’d assume would/should not be in focus for Bolt. 
{color}
* {color:#333333} *Can we sell this debt to third parties collection as a pool or as an individual debts?* 


Essentially yes, ofc market by market specifics need to be considered. 
{color}
* {color:#333333} *If not, then what case-by-case actions can be performed by Bolt for collecting outstanding amounts?* 


A debt collection framework needs to be set up which can rely more or less on internal resources, but likely we’d rather maximize the use external resources. 
{color}
* {color:#333333} *Who initiates the process of legal collection actions (either @Mart Parve or Country Manager or etc)?* 


As it’s currently envisaged then the relevant B4B account manager. 
{color}
* {color:#333333} *Based on current cases can what enforcement in an initial agreements to support better Bolt position in further legal collection actions?* 


Not sure I fully follow the question, but no cases have ever been elevated to Legal. Legal also does currently not have resources to support on the daily debt collection unless in exceptional cases (major amounts). But we have experience and can ofc support setting such procedure up. Preference should be on using external resources as said above. 
