Hi [~accountid:5ba34ceda82c5b2f3f9713e2] 

The only issue with this lease is that there is no right to terminate the contract (ever\!). There are no contractual clauses that permit Bolt to service notice to get our of the lease. This is unacceptable to us as we cannot agree to an undefined term on a lease.

Please go back to the landlord and propose the following:

{color:#6554c0}_“Bolt require a termination right to end this lease on appropriate notice (which is a market standard position). The lease provides no such right, therefore we are unable to sign it without the following clause inserted:_{color}

{color:#6554c0}*_14A - Termination for Convenience_*{color}

{color:#6554c0}*_The Tenant shall be entitled to terminate this lease by providing the Landlord with 30 days written notice of its intention to terminate. The Tenant shall only be liable for any rent payments to the Landlord on a pro-rata basis up to the date of the early termination. The Tenant shall comply with Clause 15 (End of Lease) in respect of the early termination._*{color}

{color:#6554c0}_If this can be agreed as a rider or insertion to the proposed lease, Bolt will sign the lease immediately”_{color}



The rest of the lease is generally acceptable. It's a really old version of a lease template from the law society but is satisfactory for the circumstance and given the value of the lease each year, not worth amending. As long as we can insert the termination right suggested above, I will be happy to approve this for signature.

Please can you also ask whether they can sign the lease electronically and whether we can have the name and email address of their authorised signatory.

Thanks

